  "description": "Drawing simple, conventionalised motifs in ink so a tool-cutter can engrave matching brass finishing tools. Because a single tool is impressed many times across a cover, forms are kept simple and balanced; one drawing can yield several tools at graded sizes, and leaves are usually cut in mirrored and straight variants so a pattern does not read as restless.",
